{
  "id": "80720",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Coordination Complexes in Nature and Technology",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Chlorophyll, the green pigment in plants, is a complex that contains magnesium. It is an example of a main-group element in a coordination complex. Plants appear green because chlorophyll absorbs red and purple light; the reflected light consequently appears green. The energy resulting from the absorption of light is used in photosynthesis. Many other coordination complexes are also brightly colored. The square planar copper(II) complex phthalocyanine blue is one of many complexes used as pigments or dyes. This complex is used in blue ink, blue jeans, and certain blue paints. (Why a substance has a particular color is explored in the next module.)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1969416508",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(a)"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " Chlorophyll comes in several forms, all with the same basic structure around the magnesium center. "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(b)"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " Copper phthalocyanine blue, a square planar copper complex, is in some blue dyes."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2284397491",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "2ilp53fp8t3dhse",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "display": "block",
            "id": "3608477894",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/50/506759A730F2EC1D8157D851AFB753D3/Chorophyll.jpeg",
            "type": "img",
            "width": 800
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "979400353",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "editor": "slate",
        "id": "2871380669",
        "textDirection": "ltr",
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The structure of heme, the iron-containing complex in hemoglobin, is very similar to that in chlorophyll. In hemoglobin, the red heme complex is bonded to a large protein molecule (globin) by the attachment of the protein to the heme ligand. Oxygen molecules are transported by hemoglobin in the blood by being bound to the iron center. When the hemoglobin loses its oxygen, the color changes to a bluish-red. Hemoglobin will transport oxygen only if the iron is Fe"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "2+"
              },
              {
                "text": "; oxidation of the iron to Fe"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "3+"
              },
              {
                "text": " prevents oxygen transport."
              }
            ],
            "id": "709381263",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Hemoglobin contains four protein subunits, each with an iron center attached to a heme ligand (shown in red), which is coordinated to a globin protein. Each subunit is shown in a different color."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3918998942",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "sfgzbdzs19azor6",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "display": "block",
            "height": 357,
            "id": "4099060315",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/28/283644368706DE75BD51B838B92823B4/hemoglobin.jpeg",
            "type": "img",
            "width": 433.13744075829385
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "1052098067",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "editor": "slate",
        "id": "2544604391",
        "textDirection": "ltr",
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Complexing agents are often used for water softening because they tie up ions such as Ca"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "2+"
              },
              {
                "text": ", Mg"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "2+"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and Fe"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "2+"
              },
              {
                "text": ", which make water hard. Many metal ions are also undesirable in food products because these ions can catalyze reactions that change the color of food. Coordination complexes are useful as preservatives. For example, the ligand EDTA, (HO"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "CCH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ")"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "NCH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "CH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "N(CH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "CO"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "H)"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", coordinates to metal ions through six "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "donor atoms"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A donor atom is an atom in a ligand with a lone pair of electrons that forms a coordinate covalent bond to a central metal."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2102209613",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3746428291",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " and prevents the metals from reacting (see below). This ligand is also used to sequester metal ions in paper production, textiles, and detergents and has pharmaceutical uses."
              }
            ],
            "id": "2709133374",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "The ligand EDTA binds tightly to a variety of metal ions by forming hexadentate complexes."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1859111483",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "2zfzm9pbc914kll",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "display": "block",
            "height": 383.0078125,
            "id": "2727020989",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/37/37CC7B96BAC7D13AE0DB2612F40ADFA6/EDTA binding.jpeg",
            "type": "img",
            "width": 225
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "4205761567",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "editor": "slate",
        "id": "2702951215",
        "textDirection": "ltr",
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "C﻿helation Therapy"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1955408679",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Ligands such as dimercaprol and enterobactin are important in medical treatments for heavy metal poisoning. However, chelation therapies can disrupt the normal concentration of ions in the body, leading to serious side effects, so researchers are searching for new chelation drugs. One drug that has been developed is dimercaptosuccinic acid (DMSA), shown below. Identify which atoms in this molecule could act as donor atoms."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2628477489",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "shml0rcmj8pgn6v",
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "display": "block",
                "id": "206991638",
                "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/F0/F0737A4460BD5770FA0417F93C6B11FB/DMSA.jpeg",
                "type": "img",
                "width": 500
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "S﻿olution"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3513705286",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "All the oxygen and sulfur atoms have lone pairs of electrons that can be used to coordinate to a metal center, so there are six possible donor atoms. Geometrically, only two of these atoms can be coordinated to a metal at once. The most common binding mode involves the coordination of one sulfur atom and one oxygen atom, forming a five-member ring with the metal."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "794114416",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Ligands are also used in the electroplating industry. When metal ions are reduced to produce thin metal coatings, metals can clump together to form clusters and nanoparticles. When metal coordination complexes are used, the ligands keep the metal atoms isolated from each other. It has been found that many metals plate out as a smoother, more uniform, better-looking, and more adherent surface when plated from a bath containing the metal as a complex ion. Complexes such as [Ag(CN)"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and [Au(CN)"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " are therefore used extensively in the electroplating industry."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3164061684",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "editor": "slate",
            "id": "2006449006",
            "textDirection": "ltr",
            "type": "content"
          }
